\label{lem:trinomial-ratio-revised}
Let
$
Q(y)=A_0y^a+A_1y^{a+r}+A_2y^{a+s}
$
be a polynomial with three nonzero terms and pairwise distinct
exponents in $\{0,\ldots,2M-1\}$.
Assume that
$
Q(1)=Q(\alpha)=0.
$
Then \(Q(u)\neq0\) and
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:trinomial-ratio-shifted}
\frac{Q(u^3)}{Q(u)}
=
-\alpha^a(u^{r+s}+u^r+u^s).
\end{equation}
Furthermore,
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:trinomial-not-uFq}
\frac{Q(u^3)}{Q(u)}
\notin u\mathbb F_q^*.
\end{equation}

\label{lem:single-run1}
There is no nonzero codeword of $\mathcal{C}_2$ whose support is a single cyclic run
of length at most seven.
